+++
title = "Corporate Environment Variable Resolution"
type = "specification"
scope = "corporate"
+++

# Environment Variable Resolution

## 1. Environment activation

Environment variable resolution MUST only be performed when an environment prefix (`env`) has been defined and is not empty.

If no environment prefix has been defined, environment variable lookup MUST be skipped entirely.

No implicit environment prefix MUST be assumed.

## 2. Flags

Flags are identified by a single character.

- If an explicit environment key has been defined, use that key.
- If no explicit environment key has been defined, skip environment variable lookup for that flag.

Environment keys MUST NOT be automatically generated from flag identifiers.

## 3. Parameters

For named parameters:

- If an explicit environment key has been defined, use that key.
- Otherwise, automatically derive the environment key from the parameter name.

The automatically generated environment key MUST follow this format:

```text
PREFIX_PARAMETER_NAME
```

The transformation rules are:

1. Concatenate the environment prefix and the parameter name using an underscore.
2. Replace hyphens with underscores.
3. Convert the resulting name to uppercase.

## 4. Examples

Given the environment prefix `iasi`:

| Identifier | Type | Explicit environment key | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| f | Flag | Not defined | No lookup |
| r | Flag | IASI_RECREATE_HOST | IASI_RECREATE_HOST |
| definitions | Parameter | Not defined | IASI_DEFINITIONS |
| id-host | Parameter | Not defined | IASI_ID_HOST |
| id-machines | Parameter | Not defined | IASI_ID_MACHINES |
| machines | Parameter | CUSTOM_MACHINES | CUSTOM_MACHINES |

If the environment prefix is not defined, none of these environment variables MUST be looked up.

## 5. Configuration precedence

Values obtained from environment variables MUST follow the established corporate configuration precedence.

## 6. Implementation

Environment variable resolution MUST be generic and driven by argument definitions.

Parameter-specific mappings and hardcoded environment variable names MUST NOT be introduced into the resolution mechanism.